  "verdict": "The framework's 2+1 anisotropic Lambda_mu nu structure reduces the effective time-time cosmological-constant density by Delta_Lambda/Lambda_iso = -gamma^2/(2 alpha_xi^2) = -1/162 = -0.617%, a structural first-principles correction. Integrated over the LCDM growth equation from CMB to z=0, this gives sigma_8 (anis) = 0.8118 (vs 0.811 isotropic), a relative shift of +0.098%. The mean S_8 tension across DES Y3 / KiDS-1000 / HSC Y3 is reduced by -0.036 sigma (+2.67\u03c3 -> +2.71\u03c3 on average). The shift is in the right direction but small (~0.04\u03c3); the bulk of the S_8 tension (~3\u03c3) is NOT resolved by this single structural correction. The correction is parameter-free and does not require new physics; it is the Lambda_mu nu trace deviation already documented in P4 (eq. for diag(alpha_xi^2, -gamma^2/2, -gamma^2/2, +gamma^2/2))."
